# Stray platform dirs at repo root.
#
# Per ADR-0001 the Flutter app lives entirely under apps/mobile/, so the real
# Android module is at apps/mobile/android/ and the real iOS project is at
# apps/mobile/ios/. If anyone runs `flutter pub get` (or an IDE auto-runs it)
# from the repo root by mistake, Flutter regenerates partial android/ and
# ios/ skeletons here. The skeletons are useless (no Gradle config, no
# Xcode project) but git would happily track them on the next `git add`.
#
# `/android/` and `/ios/` are anchored — they only ignore the dirs at the
# repo root. The real apps/mobile/android/ and apps/mobile/ios/ keep being
# tracked.
/android/
/ios/
